{
  "summary": "This study investigates how dual twisted interfaces in CVD-grown trilayer MoS2 affect second harmonic generation (SHG). By fabricating nine distinct stacked configurations, the researchers analyzed Raman and photoluminescence data to identify stacking-dependent phonon and excitonic responses. Atomic-resolution imaging confirmed dual twisted interfaces and a supermoiré lattice. The study developed a framework explaining SHG intensity and polarization orientation across configurations, demonstrating TT-MoS2's potential as a tunable nonlinear optical platform.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Dual twisted interfaces in trilayer MoS2 create stacking-dependent phonon and excitonic responses",
    "Atomic-resolution techniques confirmed dual twisted interfaces and a supermoiré lattice structure",
    "A framework links dual interface geometry to SHG intensity and polarization orientation"
  ],
  "study_type": "CVD-grown twisted trilayer MoS2 configurations",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a structural model for tuning nonlinear optical responses in multi-interface twisted van der Waals materials through dual interface engineering."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether piezoelectric electroporation can enhance high-frequency irreversible electroporation (H-FIRE) for prostate cancer treatment. Residual tumor cells after H-FIRE were targeted using a piezoelectric nanomaterial (BOIS) that delivers electric pulses and reactive oxygen species (ROS) to induce irreversible damage. The approach exploits DNA damage repair mechanisms to convert reversible injury into lethal outcomes, significantly improving tumor eradication without additional external energy sources.",
  "key_findings": [
    "BOIS nanomaterial delivers electric pulses and ROS to residual prostate cancer cells post-H-FIRE",
    "The dual mechanism of electroporation and oxidative stress converts reversible injury to irreversible cell death",
    "This strategy enhances H-FIRE efficacy by eliminating residual tumor cells without external energy input"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a self-reinforcing therapeutic loop where focal ablation serves as a delivery mechanism for nanomaterials, enabling targeted elimination of residual tumor cells through intrinsic electric field and oxidative stress mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study integrated single-cell epigenomic data from 2.5 million adult mouse brain nuclei to construct a comprehensive atlas of regulatory elements. It combined histone modifications, transcriptomes, chromatin accessibility, DNA methylation, and 3D genome organization to define 100+ cell subclasses and chromatin states across 81% of the genome. Active states with combinatorial histone marks better predict enhancers than accessibility alone, while H3K27me3 and H3K9me3 define repressive states. The resource enables deep learning models for predicting epigenomic features and gene expression from DNA sequences.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Integration of four histone modifications, transcriptomes, chromatin accessibility, DNA methylation, and 3D genome data across 2.5 million nuclei",
    "Identification of 100+ brain cell subclasses and chromatin states covering 81% of the genome",
    "Active chromatin states marked by combinatorial histone modifications better predict functional enhancers than chromatin accessibility alone"
  ],
  "study_type": "Single-cell epigenomic profiling",
  "scientific_significance": "This atlas provides a unified framework for annotating brain regulatory elements and interpreting non-coding disease variants through multimodal epigenomic integration."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how vascular endothelial growth factor receptor-1 (VEGFR-1) signaling maintains intestinal T follicular helper (Tfh) cell stemness to control pathobiont expansion and obesity. Conditional Flt1 deletion in T cells caused age-dependent obesity due to Taurinivorans overgrowth, which depleted host taurine and impaired adipocyte function. VEGFR-1-AKT signaling reduced Tfh senescence, preserving IgA production and gut microbiota balance.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Flt1 deletion in T cells led to age-dependent obesity via Taurinivorans overgrowth",
    "Taurinivorans depletion of host taurine suppressed adipocyte lipolysis and thermogenesis",
    "VEGFR-1-AKT signaling maintained Tfh stemness by inhibiting p53-mediated senescence"
  ],
  "study_type": "Conditional Flt1 deletion in T cells",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a VEGFR-1-dependent Tfh-microbiota axis that regulates host metabolism through IgA-mediated pathobiont control, providing a mechanistic link between immune cell senescence and metabolic disease."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of observing distributed cortical circuits during natural behavior by introducing Airscope, a 1-gram wireless mesoscope with 4 μm lateral resolution and 12.5 Hz imaging. It enables high-throughput calcium imaging of >8,500 neurons across multiple animals in diverse behavioral contexts, including social dominance, maze exploration, and fear conditioning. The technology demonstrates cortical activity patterns correlating with behavioral outcomes and spinal-cortical interactions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Airscope achieves 4 μm lateral resolution across a 6 mm field of view at 12.5 Hz with 1.0 gram weight",
    "Cortical activity patterns correlate with social dominance and competition outcomes",
    "Spinal-cortical Granger-causal influences are observed during fear conditioning"
  ],
  "study_type": "Wireless mesoscope-based imaging",
  "scientific_significance": "This technology enables large-scale, cellular-resolution cortical imaging during naturalistic behavior, advancing systems neuroscience by facilitating multi-animal studies across complex behavioral paradigms without tethering constraints."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed a deep learning biomarker, Retinal Mortality Equivalent (RetiME), using retinal photographs to predict individual mortality risk and reconstruct personalized lifespan trajectories. RetiME, validated across global cohorts, identified distinct mortality patterns linked to cancer, cardiometabolic, and neurodegenerative risks, offering a scalable method for aging-related health screening.",
  "key_findings": [
    "RetiME accurately predicts all-cause and cause-specific mortality using retinal features",
    "RetiME re-times mortality risk by reconstructing individualized lifespan trajectories",
    "Clustering revealed distinct mortality patterns associated with cancer, cardiometabolic, and neurodegenerative risks"
  ],
  "study_type": "Deep learning model trained on retinal images with external validation",
  "scientific_significance": "RetiME provides a scalable, non-invasive method to model individual mortality risk trajectories, advancing precision aging interventions through retinal imaging."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used Cas12a-based combinatorial knockout screens to investigate genetic interactions within the DNA damage response (DDR) network. By disrupting 233 DDR genes individually or in pairs, researchers identified high-confidence synthetic lethal interactions, including those between REV1-Pol ζ, MCM8-MCM9-HROB, Fanconi anusing genes, and SMARCAL1-FANCM components. These findings reveal therapeutic opportunities for tumors with specific DDR mutations.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Synthetic lethal interactions between REV1-Pol ζ and MCM8-MCM9-HROB complexes",
    "Genetic links between Fanconi anemia genes and mitotic DNA repair genes",
    "Synthetic lethality involving SMARCAL1 and FANCM complex components"
  ],
  "study_type": "Unbiased genetic interaction screens using Cas12a",
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides a comprehensive genetic map of DDR network interactions, highlighting synthetic lethal relationships that could inform targeted therapies for tumors with specific DDR mutations."
}

{
  "summary": "This study identifies a novel hematopoietic niche at the maternal-fetal interface in mice, termed MIXER, which develops alongside the yolk sac. It contains erythro-myeloid progenitors, including CSF1R+ cells and a unique eEMPROR population. Lineage tracing shows eEMPROR contributes to fetal macrophages. Human placental villi also show CD4+ nucleated erythrocytes, suggesting conserved hematopoietic activity at this interface early in development.",
  "key_findings": [
    "MIXER tissue is an early hematopoietic site at the maternal-fetal interface in mice",
    "MIXER contains CSF1R+ erythro-myeloid progenitors and eEMPROR cells",
    "eEMPROR contributes to fetal macrophage subpopulations and human placental villi harbor CD4+ nucleated erythrocytes"
  ],
  "study_type": "Mouse embryonic model",
  "scientific_significance": "This discovery reveals a conserved maternal-fetal interface as an early hematopoietic niche, expanding the understanding of blood cell origins in mammalian development."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how anisotropic van der Waals materials, specifically rhenium disulfide (ReS2), can be engineered into metasurfaces to control photonic band topology. The researchers reshaped ReS2's band structure to split topological charges into half-integer polarization singularities, creating directional flatbands. These flatbands hybridize with ReS2's excitonic transitions to form polarized exciton-polaritons, enabling polarization-resolved quantum emitters and low-threshold polariton devices.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Structuring ReS2 into a resonant metasurface splits integer topological charges into half-integer polarization singularities",
    "The engineered flatbands hybridize with ReS2's linearly polarized excitonic transitions to form directionally polarized exciton-polaritons",
    "This approach enables scalable polarization-resolved quantum emitters and flatband-enhanced nonlinear optics"
  ],
  "study_type": "Metasurface",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a pathway to manipulate photonic band topology in 2D materials for directional light-matter interactions, advancing the design of polariton-based nanophotonic devices with tailored polarization properties."
}

{
  "summary": "This commentary critiques the current AI safety discourse by highlighting that leading AI executives' recommendations emphasize AI model governance while neglecting human-AI system interactions. The study identifies a critical oversight requiring risk mitigation strategies to address the interplay between AI and human institutions, not just technical model specifications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Existing AI safety recommendations prioritize AI model safeguards over human-AI system interactions",
    "The oversight risks overlooking risks from AI interactions with people and institutions",
    "Effective AI safety requires addressing human-AI system dynamics, not isolated model governance"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This critique advances understanding of AI safety by demonstrating that multidimensional risk mitigation must encompass human-AI system interactions, not solely technical model specifications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether immune cells directly transduce mechanical cues into nociceptive signals during ulcerative colitis. Using a minimally inflammatory zymosan model, researchers identified Piezo1 in CX3CR1+ macrophages as a mechanosensor that triggers NGF synthesis via calcium influx and NF-κB nuclear translocation. This macrophage-derived NGF sensitizes TRPV1+ nociceptors, establishing a direct mechanosensory relay independent of cytokine cascades, which reduces visceral hyperalgesia when genetically disrupted.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Piezo1 in CX3CR1+ macrophages directly transduces mechanical cues into nociceptive signals during colitis",
    "Piezo1 activation induces NGF synthesis through calcium influx and NF-κB nuclear translocation",
    "Genetic disruption of Piezo1, Ngf, or Ntrk1 abolishes visceral hyperalgesia in colitis models"
  ],
  "study_type": "minimally inflammatory intracolonic zymosan model",
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies a direct mechanosensory pathway from tissue-resident macrophages to nociceptors that operates independently of inflammatory cytokines, providing a novel mechanism for visceral pain in colitis."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates closed nanopores in silicon-carbon anodes as stress-regulation units to mitigate lithiation-induced deformation and interphase degradation. By engineering heteroatom-doped carbon hosts with abundant closed pores, the material redirects expansion stress inward, reducing electrode swelling. The nitrogen-doped composite achieves 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity, 90.2% initial Coulombic efficiency, and 868.4 mAh g-1 at 3 C, with 13.1% thickness expansion after 50 cycles. This design enables scalable production and stable cycling in high-energy batteries.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Closed nanopores redirect lithiation-induced stress inward, suppressing electrode swelling",
    "Nitrogen-doped silicon-carbon composites achieve 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity",
    "The design reduces thickness expansion from 38.4% to 13.1% after 50 cycles"
  ],
  "study_type": "Material design and synthesis",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes closed-pore stress regulation as a scalable strategy for developing practical silicon-carbon anodes with minimal expansion and enhanced cycling stability in lithium-ion batteries."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed a cross-species harmonized ontology and 3: atlases for human, macaque, and marmoset basal ganglia to support the BRAIN Initiative Cell Atlas Network. It created the Harmonized Ontology of Mammalian Brain Anatomy (HOMBA) to standardize structural parcellations and enable species-specific cellular mapping within neuroimaging frameworks, facilitating comparative analyses across species.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Established HOMBA as a cross-species harmonized ontology for basal ganglia structures",
    "Generated 3D atlases for human, macaque, and marmoset basal ganglia",
    "Provided standardized frameworks for mapping cellular and molecular variations across species"
  ],
  "study_type": "Iterative approach for co-creating ontologies and atlases",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a foundational framework for cross-species neuroanatomical standardization, enabling comparative studies of cellular and molecular variations across mammalian species using unified neuroimaging coordinates."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how mitochondrial DNA (mtDNA) abundance influences immunogenic cell death (ICD) in cancer. Using KRAS-mutant cancer models, it demonstrates that MEK inhibitors induce mtDNA release but are counteracted by PRKN-mediated mitophagy. Inhibiting mitophagy enhances mtDNA efflux, amplifying cGAS-STING signaling and promoting CD8+ T cell responses. The balance between mt:cytochrome c release dictates ICD versus apoptosis outcomes, with clinical relevance in human tumors.",
  "key_findings": [
    "MEK inhibitors induce mtDNA release in KRAS-mutant cancer cells but are limited by PRKN-mediated mitophagy",
    "Inhibiting mitophagy increases mtDNA efflux, enhancing cGAS-STING signaling and CD8+ T cell activation",
    "PRKN expression negatively correlates with immune infiltration in human cancers"
  ],
  "study_type": "Preclinical models with pharmacological screening",
  "scientific_significance": "The findings establish a mechanistic link between mitochondrial dynamics, mtDNA release, and immunogenic cell death, providing a targetable pathway to enhance antitumor immunity through dual inhibition of mitochondrial stress pathways."
}

{
  "summary": "This study identifies a quadripartite functional architecture of the human insula using intracranial electrical stimulation and electroencephalography in 87 participants. It defines four regions: dorsal-posterior for nociceptive/thermoceptive signals, ventral-posterior for somatic information, mid-anterior for visceral sensations and anxiety, and anterior-polar for salience detection. The anterior region shows strong connections with the prefrontal cortex, enabling cognitive modulation of pain and bodily perception.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The insula has four distinct functional regions: dorsal-posterior encoding nociceptive/thermoceptive signals, ventral-posterior processing somatic information across body parts, mid-anterior linked to visceral sensations and anxiety, and anterior-polar involved in salience detection.",
    "The anterior-polar region exhibits strong connections with the prefrontal cortex, including the anterior cingulate cortex, exerting direct influence over other insular regions.",
    "This architecture links cytoarchitecture to asymmetric electrophysiological interactions, providing mechanistic insights into cognitive modulation of pain and interoception."
  ],
  "study_type": "Intracranial electrical stimulation and electroencephalography",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a functional framework for the human insula that connects cytoarchitectonic organization with directed electrophysiological pathways, advancing understanding of how cognition modulates pain and bodily perception."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates non-invasive vagus nerve stimulation for Parkinson's disease using an oral magnetoelectric particulate system. The system delivers magnetic field-induced electrical pulses to activate vagal afferents, engaging the brainstem and modulating dopamine and norepinephrine pathways. It reduces neuroinflammation via the cholinergic anti-inflammatory pathway, potentially alleviating motor and non-motor symptoms.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Oral delivery of magnetoeusing nickel ferrite core and barium titanate shell particles targets TRPV1 receptors for stomach adherence",
    "Magnetic field stimulation generates electrical pulses activating vagal afferents and the nucleus tractus solitarius",
    "Vagal activation enhances dopamine synthesis in substantia nigra and norepinephrine in locus coeruleus while reducing neuroinflammation"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo models",
  "scientific_significance": "This approach provides a non-invasive method to modulate Parkinson's disease pathology through gut-brain axis interactions, offering a potential therapeutic strategy without surgical intervention."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether cellular agriculture technologies can achieve cost-effective, scalable production for sustainable food systems. It evaluates enabling technologies, food functionality, and economic viability, emphasizing that manufacturing scalability and affordability are now more critical than further biological innovation for broad adoption.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Precision fermentation benefits most from functional improvements in taste, nutrition, and health rather than direct food imitation",
    "Cultivated meat production's impact will initially come from hybrid products that avoid full tissue mimicry costs",
    "Manufacturing scalability and cost efficiency are more pivotal for commercial success than continued biological technology development"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "The findings underscore that achieving scalable, affordable manufacturing processes is essential for cellular agriculture to transition from technological feasibility to widespread adoption in sustainable food systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study identifies a novel CD4-lineage erythro-myeloid progenitor (EMPROR) in adult bone marrow that generates macrophages independently of monocytes. Using single-cell RNA sequencing and lineage tracing, EMPROR cells exhibit erythroid, myeloid, and neutrophil potential while lacking Csf1r and Ccr2. The findings reveal an embryonic-like program sustaining macrophage diversity through an alternative myelopoietic pathway.",
  "key_findings": [
    "EMPROR cells generate perivascular and tumor-associated macrophages without monocyte recruitment",
    "EMPROR cells express Cd4 and Kit but lack Csf1r and Ccr2",
    "Transcriptomic data shows EMPROR cells share features with embryonic erythro-myeloid progenitors"
  ],
  "study_type": "Single-cell RNA sequencing and lineage assays",
  "scientific_significance": "The discovery of an embryonic-like erythro-myeloid progenitor in adult bone marrow reveals a previously unrecognized pathway for macrophage generation, expanding understanding of myelopoiesis beyond monocyte-dependent mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a process-intrinsic cellular network in a 3D-printed Cr-Fe-Co-Ni-Al-Ti-based multi-principal element alloy (MPEA) to achieve sustained strength-ductility across temperatures. Using laser-based additive manufacturing, the researchers designed a (CrFeCo)48Ni34Al7Ti5V5Ta1 MPEA with a self-assembled body-centred cubic/L21 precipitate network. This network enables slip transfer and back-stress hardening across specific interfaces, stabilizing deformation from 77 to 873 K. The alloy maintains yield strength above 1 GPa and uniform elongation of ~20% over this temperature range, demonstrating stable mechanical performance without post-processing.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A self-assembled body-centred cubic/L21 precipitate cellular network forms intrinsically during laser-based additive manufacturing.",
    "Slip transfer and back-stress hardening across Kurdjumov-Sachs and Nishiyama-Wassermann interfaces stabilize deformation from 77 to 873 K.",
    "The alloy maintains yield strength >1 GPa and uniform elongation of ~20% across a wide temperature range without post-processing."
  ],
  "study_type": "Laser-based additive manufacturing",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes interface-mediated plasticity mechanisms as a pathway to design strong, ductile alloys with reduced temperature sensitivity through process-intrinsic cellular networks in additive manufacturing."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the lower power conversion efficiency (PCE) and stability of flexible perovskite solar modules (PSMs) compared to rigid devices, attributed to surface hydroxyls disrupting self-assembled monolayer (SAM) anchoring. The researchers developed a decoupled SAM-perovskite codeposition strategy to accelerate SAM anchoring and improve perovskite crystallization. Certified PCE reached 20.2% on 750 cm² PSMs using phenethylammonium iodide, while a 22.0% PCE device (14.55 cm²) with 1,3-diaminopropane dihydroiodide showed 8% degradation after 1044 hours under 85°C and 65% RH.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Decoupled SAM-perovskite codeposition strategy enhances SAM anchoring and perovskite crystallization",
    "20.2% certified PCE achieved on 750 cm² flexible PSMs using phenethylammonium iodide",
    "22.0% PCE device (14.55 cm²) retained 80% efficiency after 1044 hours at 85°C and 65% RH"
  ],
  "study_type": "Decoupled SAM-perovskite codeposition strategy",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a method to overcome hydroxyl-induced instability in flexible perovskite solar cells, enabling higher efficiency and stability for commercial portable applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study evaluated human monoclonal antibodies targeting distinct MPXV epitopes to assess protective efficacy. Using a lethal vaccinia virus mouse model, researchers found that combining an anti-A35 and anti-B6 antibody provides additive and complete protection against morbidity and mortality, challenging prior assumptions about required epitope targeting for poxvirus immunity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Combination of anti-A3.5 and anti-B6 antibodies confers additive and complete protection in a lethal vaccinia mouse model",
    "Antibodies target conserved epitopes on MPXV's extracellular enveloped virion and B6 antigen",
    "The findings challenge previous assumptions that dual targeting of extracellular and mature virion forms is necessary for full protection"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vivo mouse model with lethal vaccinia virus challenge",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that targeting conserved MPXV epitopes with a single antibody combination can achieve complete protection, providing a foundation for broad-spectrum orthopoxvirus therapeutics and vaccines."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the durability challenge in rechargeable zinc-air batteries by designing a Fe-Ni dual-atom catalyst with bridging oxygen modulation. The catalyst retains 80% of initial energy efficiency after 2800 hours through multifaceted stabilization mechanisms, including reduced electron density on metal and nitrogen sites, suppressed ROS accumulation, and enhanced O-O cleavage pathways.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Fe-Ni dual-atom catalyst retains 80% initial energy efficiency after 2800 hours of operation",
    "Bridging oxygen modulates electron density to mitigate N-site protonation and metal stripping",
    "Enhanced O-O cleavage pathway suppresses H2O2 and ROS accumulation"
  ],
  "study_type": "Theoretical simulations and experimental evidence",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a coordination-engineering strategy for designing durable metal-nitrogen-carbon catalysts in zinc-air batteries, addressing critical stability issues through oxygen-mediated stabilization of dual-atom sites."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated dopamine's role in juvenile social play using naturalistic interactions. By applying social behavior sequencing, researchers identified nucleus accumbens dopamine coupling with sub-second social syllables. Findings revealed sex-divergent play strategies and disrupted dopamine signaling in Shank3-deficient autism models, with optogenetic stimulation restoring play behavior. The results highlight dopamine's critical role in orchestrating social interactions during development.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Nucleus acc: dopamine tightly coupled to sub-second social syllables during naturalistic interactions",
    "Sex-divergent dopaminergic contrast between proactive play and forced submission in wild-type juveniles",
    "Abolished proactive play-evoked dopamine responses in Shank3-deficient males, with sign-inverted responses in females"
  ],
  "study_type": "Social behavior sequencing (Social-seq) analysis",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes sub-second dopamine reinforcement as a fundamental mechanism governing naturalistic social behavior, offering a potential intervention framework for neurodevelopmental disorders through targeted dopaminergic modulation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how tumor cells reprogrammed into conventional dendritic cell type 1 (cDC1)-like cells induce immunogenic lymphoid structures within tumors across multiple cancer types. The research demonstrates that these reprogrammed cells remodel the tumor microenvironment, activate immune signaling pathways, and form germinal centers, leading to systemic anti-tumor immunity without requiring endogenous cDC1s. The findings highlight a potential mechanism for overcoming immunotherapy resistance.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Reprogrammed tumor cells into cDC1-like cells induced immunogenic lymphoid structures across five cancer models",
    "cDC1-like cells activated lymphotoxin, TN: TNF, and interferon programs to engage T cells via MHC class I and CD40 signaling",
    "ImgTLSs promoted systemic immunity through expansion of shared T and B cell clonotypes in distant tumors"
  ],
  "study_type": "Preclinical mouse and human tumor models",
  "scientific_significance": "The study establishes cDC1-like cell reprogramming as a universal mechanism for initiating intratumoral lymphoid structures that can overcome immunotherapy resistance across diverse cancer types."
}
